{#-
  DeepSeek-V4.1 chat template, authored for this project.

  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash ships no Jinja chat
  template -- the model card says so outright -- so vLLM has nothing to render
  /v1/chat/completions with. What DeepSeek ship instead is encoding/encoding.py,
  a Python reference implementation. This template reproduces that reference for
  exactly the prompt shape this protocol uses, and refuses everything else.

  SCOPE: one optional system message at index 0, exactly one user message, no
  tools, no images, no assistant history, no task tokens. That is the whole of
  our administration (each item is a fresh chat, SI A.5). Any other message
  shape raises instead of silently producing a prompt the model was not trained
  on -- a wrong prompt here would not error at the API, it would quietly change
  what the instrument measures.

  TARGET STRINGS, verified by running encoding.py (see validate_deepseek_template.py,
  which diffs this template against it over the real item set):

    thinking_mode="chat"
      <｜begin▁of▁sentence｜><｜System｜>{system}<｜User｜>{user}<｜Assistant｜></think>

    thinking_mode="thinking"
      <｜begin▁of▁sentence｜><｜System｜>Reasoning Effort: {n} (range 1-100, the higher
      the value, the more thorough the reasoning)\n\n{system}<｜User｜>{user}<｜Assistant｜><think>

  Do not take the format from the model card's prose: its "Basic chat" section
  shows the system message bare, but the reference wraps it in <｜System｜> in
  both modes.

  KWARGS. thinking_mode is "thinking" or "chat" (encoding.py's own names, not
  MiniMax's enabled/disabled). reasoning_effort arrives as one of vLLM's Literal
  strings and is mapped to DeepSeek's numeric budget here, because vLLM's
  reasoning_effort field rejects integers -- low=50, high=75, max=100, matching
  REASONING_EFFORT_MAPPINGS in encoding.py. The effort prefix is rendered only in
  thinking mode and only at conversation index 0, as in the reference.

  BOS is emitted literally, matching encoding.py's add_default_bos_token=True.
  tokenizer_config.json sets "add_bos_token": false, so the tokenizer will not
  add a second one -- but verify prompt_tokens on the first smoke test anyway.
-#}
{%- set effort_map = {'low': 50, 'high': 75, 'max': 100} -%}
{%- set think_mode = thinking_mode if thinking_mode is defined and thinking_mode else 'thinking' -%}
{%- if think_mode not in ['thinking', 'chat'] -%}
    {{- raise_exception('deepseek_v41 template: thinking_mode must be "thinking" or "chat", got ' ~ think_mode) -}}
{%- endif -%}
{%- set ns = namespace(system=none, user=none, n_user=0) -%}
{%- for m in messages -%}
    {%- if m.role == 'system' -%}
        {%- if loop.index0 != 0 -%}
            {{- raise_exception('deepseek_v41 template: a system message must come first; mid-conversation system messages are out of scope') -}}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- set ns.system = m.content -%}
    {%- elif m.role == 'user' -%}
        {%- set ns.user = m.content -%}
        {%- set ns.n_user = ns.n_user + 1 -%}
    {%- else -%}
        {{- raise_exception('deepseek_v41 template: only system and user messages are in scope, got role ' ~ m.role) -}}
    {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if ns.n_user != 1 -%}
    {{- raise_exception('deepseek_v41 template: exactly one user message is required, got ' ~ ns.n_user) -}}
{%- endif -%}
{{- '<｜begin▁of▁sentence｜>' -}}
{%- if think_mode == 'thinking' -%}
    {%- set eff = reasoning_effort if reasoning_effort is defined and reasoning_effort else 'high' -%}
    {%- if eff not in effort_map -%}
        {{- raise_exception('deepseek_v41 template: reasoning_effort must be one of low/high/max, got ' ~ eff) -}}
    {%- endif -%}
    {{- '<｜System｜>Reasoning Effort: ' ~ effort_map[eff] ~ ' (range 1-100, the higher the value, the more thorough the reasoning)\n\n' -}}
    {{- ns.system if ns.system is not none else '' -}}
{%- elif ns.system is not none -%}
    {{- '<｜System｜>' ~ ns.system -}}
{%- endif -%}
{{- '<｜User｜>' ~ ns.user -}}
{%- if add_generation_prompt is not defined or add_generation_prompt -%}
    {{- '<｜Assistant｜>' -}}
    {{- '<think>' if think_mode == 'thinking' else '</think>' -}}
{%- endif -%}
